::ENG4_U03_L08_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.R.05] Passage: A city proposal begins by explaining a public access problem, then presents a limited pilot program, then describes how officials will measure demand. Which structure is used?
{
=B. Problem-solution with evaluation.#Correct
~A. Chronological personal narrative.#Incorrect
~C. Fictional conflict and resolution.#Incorrect
~D. Unrelated description.#Incorrect
}
::ENG4_U03_L08_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.R.06] Passage: The claim is that public charging stations would help transit riders. Evidence includes digital tickets, route updates, job communication, and emergency contact. How effective is the evidence?
{
~B. Ineffective because phone use is unrelated to transit.#Incorrect
=A. Effective because it connects charging access to practical rider needs.#Correct
~C. Ineffective because all evidence must be numerical.#Incorrect
~D. Effective only because it mentions jobs.#Incorrect
}
::ENG4_U03_L08_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.R.07] Passage: A county message uses calm language, clear steps, and a limited rollout to persuade officials. What purpose does this approach serve?
{
~A. To make the proposal seem irresponsible.#Incorrect
~B. To entertain readers with humor.#Incorrect
=C. To present the proposal as manageable and measurable.#Correct
~D. To avoid making a recommendation.#Incorrect
}
::ENG4_U03_L08_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.R.08] Text A uses survey data to support evening internet access. Text B uses a worker's story about missing an online deadline. Which comparison is strongest?
{
=D. Text A builds broad evidence, while Text B humanizes the impact.#Correct
~B. Text B is unrelated because it lacks survey data.#Incorrect
~C. Text A is emotional because it has data.#Incorrect
~A. Both texts use identical rhetoric.#Incorrect
}
::ENG4_U03_L08_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.R.12] Passage: "This pilot is not a permanent expansion; it is a measured test of community need." What is the rhetorical effect?
{
~A. It makes the plan seem careless.#Incorrect
=B. It reduces concern by framing the plan as limited and evidence-driven.#Correct
~C. It creates a hostile tone.#Incorrect
~D. It removes the author's purpose.#Incorrect
}
